[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64702,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Squamous papillomas are rare benign squamous epithelial proliferations commonly detected as multiple papillomas in the vulvar vestibule or vagina.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64703,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8052/0 Squamous cell papilloma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64704,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GA14.0 &amp; XH50T2 Polyp of vagina &amp; Squamous cell papilloma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64705,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> vestibular papillomatosis; hirsuties papillaris vulvae; micropapillomatosis labialis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64706,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vestibular micropapillomatosis; solitary vaginal papilloma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64707,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Micropapillomatosis typically occurs in the distal vagina and around the introitus vaginae (vulvar vestibule) in a linear and symmetrical distribution, as part of normal variation. The rare solitary squamous papilloma occurs most commonly in the lateral walls of the distal vagina.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64708,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Micropapillomatosis comprises pink, asymptomatic, painless, fine projections of vestibular epithelium. Solitary papillomas are larger pedunculated proliferations. They are most often discovered in young girls and young women.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64709,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are insufficient epidemiological data.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64710,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology of solitary squamous papilloma and micropapillomatosis is unknown but is unrelated to HPV infection {2175164; 7566844}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64711,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64712,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Squamous papilloma of the vagina is usually a pedunculated papillomatous lesion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64713,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Solitary squamous papillomas have a thin, delicate fibrovascular stalk and are covered by mature glycogenated squamous epithelium. Parakeratosis and hyperkeratosis, koilocytes, mitoses, and atypia are absent. There are two subtypes: the more common vestibular micropapillomatosis {30144403} and the less common solitary vaginal papilloma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64714,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64715,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64716,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 330,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> papilloma with a fibrovascular stalk covered by mature glycogenated squamous epithelium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:54:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
